      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T14:09:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "* Sounds reasonable, but see below.\n* I agree.\n* Some GPUs don\u0027t support integers -- again I\u0027m hoping we can avoid those architectures. Also, because we pack the texture index in the the u value, we\u0027re maxed out to 4K textures. Due to precision issues, we\u0027re maxed out to 2K in some cases (Mali 400 *shakes tiny fist*).",
      "parentUuid": "0ea97408_ea8a67ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ac2ebf4_f7eb2b45",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/TextDirectRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T14:43:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would also hope that we can get away from GPUs that don\u0027t support integers, but if we have a gles2 fallback, that may not be possible. \n\nIf we need to, I think this would be addressed by having the RenderSteps created by the Context during initialization, and we can then choose to use the ushort or float texCoord variant based on what the GPU supports.",
      "parentUuid": "600fea3f_29a8b097",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47bc898b_f69aaa15",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/TextDirectRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T13:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At this point in the Graphite DrawPass processing pipeline, the SkPaint will unaccessible, unless SubRunData is explicitly holding on to it.\n\nIf the only thing it needs from the paint is whether or not it\u0027s solid color, I\u0027d say we just track that optional color and not the whole paint. That said, I have some thoughts on how we should do the solid color optimizations in graphite, that I put in a previous comment.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1871e902_b8a17b59",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/TextDirectRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T14:09:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Ganesh (and I guess raster), color emoji and masks handle the color differently. Color emoji extracts the alpha from the SkPaint and modulates only that with the texture data; masks modulate the full color. I\u0027d prefer if we didn\u0027t special case that -- if they want only alpha to be applied to the mask they should use white with that alpha, but I\u0027m not sure what clients depend on it. In any case, to handle this, the \"drawingColor\" is packed into the AtlasTextOp Geometry, and could be stored in the SubRunData in the same way.",
      "parentUuid": "47bc898b_f69aaa15",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f850866_4e1647a5",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/render/TextDirectRenderStep.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T14:43:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This behavior sounds equivalent to what we do if there\u0027s an SkShader or paint color combined with a drawImage call. We use just the alpha from the paint color or paint shader and combine it with the texture data. This makes sense if we assume emoji are effectively textures being drawn in glyph locations, whereas the mask being in a texture is just an implementation detail for how we get the glyph coverage, so we treat the rest of the painting/shading as if it were a non-texture draw.",
      "parentUuid": "1871e902_b8a17b59",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "821733b2_48fae54b",
        "filename": "src/text/gpu/SubRunContainer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1596,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-01T13:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It wouldn\u0027t take too much work to make this possible, but this use pattern relies on a patterned index buffer having been created. I didn\u0027t have DrawWriter support it initially since almost all cases where we do use that in Ganesh, we\u0027d be better off doing instances, which can be done with DrawWriter::Instances + optional fixed vertex and index buffers for the instance pattern.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1595,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 1596,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "487bd7a8aac1049e34efcf1921a8672f9f1d0531",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12be1091_25ad2f72",
        "filename": "src/text/gpu/SubRunContainer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1596,
